I suppose it might be &quot;bad form&quot;, but couldn&#x27;t you, if you had:<p><pre><code>  public interface FooBar
  {
     int foo();
     int bar();
  }
  public Afob implements FooBar {...}
</code></pre>
refactor FooBar to simply:<p><pre><code>    public interface Foo { int foo() }
    public interface Bar { int bar() }
    public interface FooBar extends Foo, Bar {}
</code></pre>
And keep FooBar the way it was, but now cast it to a Foo (or Bar) when you don&#x27;t want a FooBar?
